      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During its heyday, Mineral hosted fifteen gold mines within two miles, making it the center of gold mining in Louisa County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A zinc and lead mine kept working in Mineral into the 1970s, extending the town’s mining legacy well beyond gold.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Virginia Central Railroad built its first depot in Mineral in 1851, and the current station stands on that original site.",
